 b.C(188,[212],P,[121],'647-651','Every morphism of the stated admissible generalized theories is already a τ∞ quasi-isomorphism.','formal consequence of the comparison axioms, conditional on the proposed τ∞ formalism','E','A natural morphism respecting the constant augmentation commutes with the comparison diagram. Once both comparison arrows are isomorphisms, two-out-of-three proves the claim. Cartan comparison and Mandell2002 provide neighboring precise axioms; neither repairs the separate early τ∞ definition automatically.',[CA,'Mandell2002'],'Formal commutative-diagram argument in mathematical_checks.md; no finite computation.','high','MID-S08,MID-S14,MID-S26–28,MID-S36')
