 b.C(193,[221],P,[109],'400-405','A minimal model is built by adding generators successively to make H^n surjective and kill the kernel in H^(n+1), sometimes in infinitely many steps.','English donor exposition, not securely attributed','B','Sullivan1977 §5 pp.288–289 gives exactly this add-and-kill construction for H^0 equal to the ground field, including repeated degree-one-driven steps and the generalized nilpotent outcome. The original leaf’s date and authorship remain unknown.',['Sullivan1977'],confidence='high',search='MID-S16,MID-S19,MID-S20,MID-S36–38')
 b.C(194,[221],P,[109],'398-405','The degree-one submodel determines nilpotent quotients of π1 over Q or R.','English donor assertion, with omitted surrounding hypotheses','C','Sullivan1977 Theorem8.1(ii), p.301, identifies the fundamental group of a nilpotent finite-type realization with the rational nilpotent group of the dual Lie algebra. §5 p.289 and §8 p.303 discuss generalized nilpotent/infinite versions. This supports the rational nilpotent content but does not license tensoring an arbitrary nonabelian group as an ordinary module.',['Sullivan1977'],confidence='medium: precise interpretation depends on the missing preceding English pages',search='MID-S16,MID-S19,MID-S20,MID-S36–38')
 b.C(195,[221],P,[109],'406-411','The model gives a tower of principal rational Eilenberg–Mac Lane fibrations, described as the rational homotopy type for all fundamental groups.','English donor assertion qualified by its next paragraph','C','Sullivan1977 §8 pp.301–303 constructs realization fibrations from algebra extensions and remarks on canonical rational/real Postnikov systems. Its equivalence with homotopy groups of the original space has nilpotent/finiteness or continuous-dual qualifications. A generalized nilpotent model exists for arbitrary connected input; it is not automatically the unrestricted homotopy type.',['Sullivan1977'],confidence='medium',search='MID-S16,MID-S19,MID-S20,MID-S36–38')
